> Why would this be possible? You say that your god should be on friendly
> terms with you, so undoubtedly he must be involved in the making of the
> altar. Why then would he create a non-coaligned altar?

Because you are confused *and* hallucinating while praying, which on the 
one hand is necessary to get you in the right state of mind to be able 
to create an altar at all but on the other hand may make you pray to the 
wrong god.  "Being confused, you pray to Loki instead to Odin..."

Since in nethack there is only three incarnations of one deity, you can 
say that being on friendly terms with your god means being on 
sufficiently friendly terms with all three that if you release the 
spiritual power that results in demanding the creation of an altar, any 
one will respond positively...  But since the deity is schizophrenic 
(has multiple personalities), one of them can be pissed off afterwards, 
and then of course, all of them are.  (I think, it works this way.  If 
you anger your god and put on a helm of opposite alignment, you still 
cannot pray safely to the other god.)

Of course, one could change this to a more reasonable setting, if the 
nethack deities were more cleanly separated.  Then you would have to be 
on friendly terms with the god you are actually praying to in your 
confused state (which might be difficult for other gods than your own...)
